### Parser reads day-first dates as month-first

The shared parser reads every date month-first. For day-first tenants, that flips the date. These reports arrived through app, email, and form channels. Intake tags are only a guess; use tenant locale to classify the reports.

### Booking-v3 date hint conflicts with tenant locale

These reports came through booking-v3 forms. The form displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, while the tenants use day-first locales. People follow the hint, then the form interprets the value using the tenant's day-first order and flips it. Use the tenant locale and form configuration to classify the reports; intake tags are only a guess.

## Engineering update · 5 October

The support desk closed #4471 on 5 October. Engineering fixed the parser cause with `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The booking-v3 hint cause will not be fixed because the booking-v3 form was retired.

